The greatest common divisor ($GCD$) and the least common multiple ($LCM$) of two integers can be found using the following formulas:

/* $gcd(x, y)$ */ $gcd = x$ if $y = 0$ else $gcd(y, x \mod y)$
/* $lcm(x, y)$ */ $lcm = |x \times y| / gcd(x, y)$

To find the $GCD$ and $LCM$ of $50$ and $5005$, we first find the $GCD$. The $GCD$ of $50$ and $5005$ is $5$. Next, we find the $LCM$. Using the formula $lcm = |x \times y| / gcd(x, y)$, we get $lcm = |50 \times 5005| / 5 = 50050$.</think> <answer>$50100$</answer>

